{
  "id": "27994_koushinsuru",
  "headword": "{更新|こうしん}する",
  "reading": "こうしんする",
  "romaji": "koushinsuru",
  "part_of_speech": "suru verb",
  "gloss": "to update; to renew; to break (a record)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to update; to renew; to break (a record)",
      "explanation": "To replace something with a newer version or state — updating data or software, renewing a contract or license, or setting a new record that surpasses the previous one."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27994_koushinsuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "アプリを{最新版|さいしんばん}に{更新|こうしん}した。",
      "english": "I updated the app to the latest version.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27994_koushinsuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{運転|うんてん}{免許|めんきょ}を{更新|こうしん}する。",
      "english": "to renew one's driver's license.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27994_koushinsuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{彼女|かのじょ}は{世界|せかい}{記録|きろく}を{更新|こうしん}した。",
      "english": "She broke the world record.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27994_koushinsuru_ex4",
      "japanese": "ウェブサイトの{情報|じょうほう}を{毎日|まいにち}{更新|こうしん}して、{最新|さいしん}の{状態|じょうたい}に{保|たも}っている。",
      "english": "I update the website's information daily to keep it current.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Transitive ({他動詞|たどうし}); the noun {更新|こうしん} takes する. Covers replacing with something newer (data, software), renewing (contracts, licenses), and surpassing a previous record.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {記録|きろく}を{更新|こうしん}する: to break a record\n- {契約|けいやく}を{更新|こうしん}する: to renew a contract\n- データを{更新|こうしん}する: to update data\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {新|あたら}しくする: to make new — plainer and more general\n- {改|あらた}める: to revise; to change — emphasizes correcting rather than renewing",
